WEBVTT

00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:10.300
Sorry I'm late,

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.277
but I have a very good excuse.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.677
Picture this:

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.840
I'm just getting ready
to leave the Mess Hall

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.180
when Ensign Wildman
goes into labor.

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:20.880
What else could I do
but deliver the baby?

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.547
Oh, you should
have been there, Harry.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:25.854
There is nothing like bringing
a new life into the world.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.587
I think I missed my calling.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.989
What if I told you

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:33.294
the turbolift got stuck
on Deck 6?

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.198
This is the third time
you've been late this week,

00:00:35.235 --> 00:00:36.293
Mr. Paris.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.463
It won't happen again.

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:41.440
Commander, I am picking up
a distress call

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.998
on one of the upper
subspace bands.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.303
What's the source?

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.834
A small spacecraft.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:47.210
No weapon systems.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.874
One life-form aboard.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.576
Extremely weak life signs.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:51.879
Slow to half impulse.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.751
According to the bioscanner,
it's a Vidiian female.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.517
Open a channel.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.148
No response.

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.556
She may be too sick.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.694
Or maybe
it's some kind of trick.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:05.664
Preliminary scans show no other
Vidiian ships in this sector.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.632
It is unlikely
that this is a trap.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.362
Commander Chakotay,
notify the Doctor.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.267
Mr. Kim, beam the woman
to Sick Bay.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.498
Aye, Captain.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:24.350
Her renal organs

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.545
are functioning
at 20 percent of normal

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.248
and her cardiovascular system
is on the verge of collapse.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.917
20 milligrams of lectrazine.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:41.392
Cardiovascular and renal
systems are stabilizing,

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.402
but her neural patterns
are fading.

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.772
What is it?

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:51.936
In her parietal lobe.

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.139
It looks like
some sort of implant.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:01.014
It's a very complex web
of bio-neural circuitry,

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.316
nano-fibers.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:04.687
Could this be
what's causing the problem?

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.351
On the contrary.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.916
According to these readings,

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.896
the device is actually
storing her synaptic patterns,

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.227
processing them

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.165
and transmitting
neuro-electrical impulses

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.667
to the rest of her systems.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.105
Are you saying it's some kind
of artificial brain?

00:02:24.144 --> 00:02:26.271
No.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.770
I'd say it's more like
a neuro-cortical stimulator

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:32.478
designed to supplement
the higher brain functions.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.248
But it's not working anymore.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:37.518
From what I can tell, the
implant itself is functioning,

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.548
but it's connected
to mostly dead nerve cells.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.355
If we don't do something
quickly,

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.828
she'll be brain dead
in a matter of minutes.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.559
What about trying to stimulate
cell regeneration

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.567
with a high dosage
of inaprovaline?

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.159
Very impressive, Kes,

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.103
but I think
it's too late for that.

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:55.734
Get me a high-frequency
RF transmitter.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:58.005
You're going to have
to hurry, Kes.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:03:00.035
The patient's brain function
is diminishing rapidly.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:07.347
Now... set
the delta band frequency

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:10.413
of the holo-emitter
to 8.6 tetrahertz.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.048
What are we doing, exactly?

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.820
Transferring the patient's
synaptic patterns

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.987
into the holo-buffer
before they degrade completely.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:19.558
Is there enough storage capacity

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.965
in the holo-matrix for such
complex data patterns?

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:24.366
There's enough capacity
for my program, isn't there?

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:27.965
And my program contains over
50 million gigaquads of data,

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.975
which, I don't have to tell you,
is considerably more

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:32.204
than the most highly-developed
humanoid brains.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.577
What good is preserving
her synaptic patterns

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.377
if there is no body?

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:38.077
I'm creating a holographic body.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.813
Not only will we be able
to communicate

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.821
with the patient, but we'll
have an accurate model

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:43.879
of healthy Vidiian

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:46.448
physiology that will aid
in treating her actual body.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:50.690
Computer, project the patient's
skeletal structure.

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.463
Now add internal organs.

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.795
Add musculature.

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.973
Now apply epidermal layers.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.508
Computer,
use transporter records

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.949
to recreate
the patient's clothing.

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:15.939
According to her ship's
navigational logs,

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:19.204
the woman was en route
to a remote Vidiian colony.

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:20.473
Are we anywhere near it?

00:06:20.513 --> 00:06:22.378
It's about ten light-years away.

00:06:22.414 --> 00:06:25.577
We should be in the general
vicinity in about 22 days.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:26.778
Assuming she survives

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:29.447
and we can take adequate
security precautions,

00:06:29.488 --> 00:06:32.116
we'll turn her over to her
people when we get there.

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.750
Captain.

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:35.350
Is there something wrong?

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:38.158
I wanted to talk to you
about Lieutenant Paris.

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:41.462
His attitude lately's been
less than professional.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.434
I've noticed.

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:46.063
I know crew discipline's
my responsibility,

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:49.472
but, in this case, I thought
I should let you get involved

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:50.975
before I took any action.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.102
In a way, Paris has been

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:53.736
your personal
reclamation project.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:58.311
I appreciate your bringing this
to my attention, Commander,

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:02.514
but I trust you to handle
the problem any way you see fit.

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:12.287
Chief Medical Officer's Log,
supplemental.

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:13.662
Test results indicate

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:16.327
that the holographic body
is functioning normally.

00:07:16.368 --> 00:07:18.893
The patient's synaptic patterns
appear to be stable,

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:21.099
so I'm now ready
to begin transferring

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.199
her cognitive
and motor processes.

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:41.092
Who are you?

00:07:41.225 --> 00:07:42.852
I'm the Chief Medical Officer

00:07:42.893 --> 00:07:45.088
of the Federation Starship
Voyager.

00:07:45.129 --> 00:07:47.927
We received your distress call
and brought you aboard.

00:07:56.307 --> 00:07:57.774
What have you done to me?

00:07:57.808 --> 00:07:59.139
It's quite simple really.

00:07:59.176 --> 00:08:01.337
I used the undamaged
chromosomes in your cerebellum

00:08:01.378 --> 00:08:03.869
to recreate
your original DNA code,

00:08:03.914 --> 00:08:05.404
and then programmed the computer

00:08:05.449 --> 00:08:08.612
to project a holographic
template based on that genome.

00:08:08.652 --> 00:08:10.517
Holographic?

00:08:10.554 --> 00:08:14.320
A three-dimensional projection
of light and energy.

00:08:14.358 --> 00:08:16.553
See for yourself.

00:08:32.576 --> 00:08:34.942
Your neural patterns
were degrading rapidly.

00:08:34.979 --> 00:08:36.071
It was too late

00:08:36.113 --> 00:08:37.876
to expect results
from inaprovaline,

00:08:37.915 --> 00:08:40.406
so I was forced to improvise,

00:08:40.451 --> 00:08:43.784
not that it would have occurred
to just any physician.

00:08:50.794 --> 00:08:53.558
Why are you crying?

00:08:55.199 --> 00:08:57.099
I'm sorry. I...

00:08:57.134 --> 00:08:58.761
I thought you'd be pleased.

00:08:58.802 --> 00:09:00.167
I am.

00:09:01.972 --> 00:09:04.907
I just never expected
to look healthy again.

00:09:04.975 --> 00:09:07.500
I've been sick for so long.

00:09:11.148 --> 00:09:13.446
I'll need
a complete medical history.

00:09:13.484 --> 00:09:15.042
How long have you
been ill exactly?

00:09:15.085 --> 00:09:18.521
I was first diagnosed
with the phage when I was seven.

00:09:18.556 --> 00:09:21.582
And when did you begin receiving
replacement tissue?

00:09:21.625 --> 00:09:23.388
About that same time.

00:09:23.427 --> 00:09:25.122
At first, it was hard
to get used to the changes,

00:09:25.162 --> 00:09:27.926
but it happened so often
that after a while,

00:09:28.032 --> 00:09:29.795
I almost stopped noticing.

00:09:29.833 --> 00:09:31.357
I-I never...

00:09:33.470 --> 00:09:36.200
I never thought
I'd see myself again.

00:09:40.911 --> 00:09:43.311
Thank you.

00:09:43.347 --> 00:09:45.178
This is the most
extraordinary thing

00:09:45.216 --> 00:09:46.706
anyone has ever done for me.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:47.944
I wouldn't be too grateful.

00:09:48.052 --> 00:09:50.612
There are serious limitations
to being a hologram.

00:09:50.654 --> 00:09:53.122
First of all, we can only exist
within environments

00:09:53.157 --> 00:09:56.422
equipped with holo-emitters,
such as this Sick Bay.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:09:58.428
You mean, you're...

00:09:58.462 --> 00:10:00.623
I'm this ship's emergency
medical holographic program.

00:10:00.664 --> 00:10:03.155
You're a computer simulation?

00:10:04.335 --> 00:10:08.066
An incredibly sophisticated
computer simulation.

00:10:08.105 --> 00:10:09.436
I'm sorry.

00:10:12.309 --> 00:10:14.209
What did you say your name was?

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.541
I don't have a name.

00:10:18.582 --> 00:10:20.607
It wasn't part
of my original program.

00:10:20.651 --> 00:10:23.381
However, you, I'm sure,
have one.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:25.115
Danara.

00:10:25.155 --> 00:10:26.452
Danara Pel.

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:27.650
Well, Miss Pel,

00:10:27.691 --> 00:10:29.955
may I ask what someone
with an illness like yours

00:10:29.994 --> 00:10:32.622
was doing alone in space
with no access to medical care?

00:10:32.663 --> 00:10:33.755
I was helping to treat

00:10:33.797 --> 00:10:35.788
an outbreak of the phage
on Fina Prime.

00:10:35.833 --> 00:10:37.892
I was on my way
back to my home colony,

00:10:37.935 --> 00:10:40.665
but it's a long journey
and my condition got worse.

00:10:40.704 --> 00:10:43.172
You're a medical practitioner
of some kind?

00:10:43.207 --> 00:10:44.469
A hematologist.

00:10:44.508 --> 00:10:46.999
Well, then, perhaps,
given your expertise,

00:10:47.111 --> 00:10:49.136
you can help me
with your treatment.

00:10:49.179 --> 00:10:51.113
My treatment?

00:10:51.148 --> 00:10:52.979
I feel fine.

00:10:53.017 --> 00:10:54.712
Unfortunately,
that's only temporary.

00:10:54.752 --> 00:10:56.686
Your synaptic patterns
will eventually degrade

00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:58.347
if we don't get them out
of the pattern buffers

00:10:58.389 --> 00:10:59.356
and back into your brain.

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:00.516
How long?

00:11:00.557 --> 00:11:02.548
A few days.
Perhaps a week.

00:11:02.593 --> 00:11:04.083
I see.

00:11:04.128 --> 00:11:06.358
Your real body is in stasis.

00:11:06.397 --> 00:11:08.490
As you can see,
we have to find a way

00:11:08.532 --> 00:11:09.897
to repair
your damaged neural tissue.

00:11:14.405 --> 00:11:15.770
Is something wrong?

00:11:17.074 --> 00:11:18.405
It's nothing.

00:11:18.442 --> 00:11:20.467
I'm eager to discuss treatments.

00:11:20.511 --> 00:11:21.978
Of course.

00:11:35.959 --> 00:11:37.221
The procedure is quite simple.

00:11:37.261 --> 00:11:38.990
I'll drill an opening
into your skull

00:11:39.029 --> 00:11:41.190
precisely two millimeters
in diameter,

00:11:41.231 --> 00:11:42.698
and then use a neuralyte probe

00:11:42.733 --> 00:11:44.598
to extract a sample
of your parietal lobe

00:11:44.635 --> 00:11:46.000
weighing
approximately one gram.

00:11:46.070 --> 00:11:48.231
It doesn't sound simple to me.

00:11:48.272 --> 00:11:49.569
I still have nightmares

00:11:49.606 --> 00:11:51.164
about what those people
did to me.

00:11:51.208 --> 00:11:53.472
And now you want
to crack open my head,

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:55.273
cut out a piece of my brain

00:11:55.312 --> 00:11:56.574
and give it to her?

00:11:56.613 --> 00:11:58.513
Your experience
in the Vidiian prison

00:11:58.549 --> 00:12:01.643
suggests Klingon DNA
is resistant to the phage.

00:12:01.685 --> 00:12:04.347
Losing a small amount of neural
tissue is inconsequential.

00:12:04.388 --> 00:12:05.355
Not to me, it isn't.

00:12:05.389 --> 00:12:06.822
Yet that same tissue,

00:12:06.857 --> 00:12:09.519
grafted onto the patient's brain
and stimulated to grow,

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:12.188
will significantly slow
the spread of her infection.

00:12:12.229 --> 00:12:14.390
If we can increase the grafted
tissue mass quickly enough,

00:12:14.431 --> 00:12:16.456
we can transfer
her synaptic patterns

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:18.968
back into her brain before they
degrade in the holo-buffer.

00:12:19.069 --> 00:12:20.559
It won't cure the phage,

00:12:20.604 --> 00:12:23.630
but it should
prolong her life considerably.

00:12:23.674 --> 00:12:25.699
Please change
into a surgical gown

00:12:25.743 --> 00:12:26.903
and lie down
on bio-bed number one.

00:12:26.944 --> 00:12:27.911
I am not going...

00:12:27.945 --> 00:12:29.344
Excuse me.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.581
I just want to say that...

00:12:34.618 --> 00:12:36.779
I've read about the experiments
that were done on you.

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:38.981
What you went through
must have been very traumatic.

00:12:39.089 --> 00:12:40.818
That is an understatement.

00:12:40.858 --> 00:12:42.291
I'm sure it is.

00:12:42.326 --> 00:12:44.590
Please understand, this disease

00:12:44.628 --> 00:12:46.926
has been killing my people
for hundreds of years.

00:12:46.964 --> 00:12:49.558
Trying to stop it
has become an obsession

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:51.329
and many of our politicians
and scientists

00:12:51.368 --> 00:12:52.426
have never developed

00:12:52.469 --> 00:12:55.495
compassion for the people
who keep us alive.

00:12:55.539 --> 00:12:58.406
As much as I want
to go on living,

00:12:58.442 --> 00:13:01.434
I have accepted the fact
that I will die soon.

00:13:03.347 --> 00:13:07.249
I only want your help
if you are willing to give it.

00:13:09.153 --> 00:13:13.852
Of course, I... I'd like
to help you if I can.

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:19.486
If you have any questions at all
about the procedure,

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:23.330
I'd... I'd be happy
to answer them for you.

00:13:27.971 --> 00:13:30.303
I'll go and get changed.

00:13:36.313 --> 00:13:39.180
I've finished ingrafting
the Klingon neural tissue

00:13:39.216 --> 00:13:40.683
to your cerebral cortex.

00:13:40.717 --> 00:13:42.981
Now, all I have to do
is create an axonal pathway

00:13:43.053 --> 00:13:45.283
between that tissue
and your basal ganglia.

00:13:45.322 --> 00:13:47.085
Your technique
is very impressive.

00:13:47.124 --> 00:13:48.819
It's all part
of my programming.

00:13:48.859 --> 00:13:50.724
For example, this exact
procedure was developed

00:13:50.761 --> 00:13:53.229
by Dr. Leonard McCoy
in the year 2253.

00:13:53.263 --> 00:13:55.356
I'm equipped with
the collective medical knowledge

00:13:55.399 --> 00:13:57.799
of more than 3,000 cultures.

00:13:57.835 --> 00:14:00.633
Additionally, as you see here,

00:14:00.671 --> 00:14:03.572
my imaging system
allows me to perform

00:14:03.607 --> 00:14:04.938
and, in many cases, improve upon

00:14:05.008 --> 00:14:07.203
the most delicate
tactile maneuvers

00:14:07.244 --> 00:14:10.338
required by a dizzying array
of surgical procedures.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:11.574
Incredible.

00:14:11.615 --> 00:14:12.741
It is, isn't it?

00:14:12.783 --> 00:14:15.616
Hand me the submicron
suture, please.

00:14:19.289 --> 00:14:21.018
There. That should do it.

00:14:22.025 --> 00:14:24.118
Ah. Excellent work, Doctor.

00:14:24.161 --> 00:14:25.856
I was only assisting.

00:14:25.896 --> 00:14:27.693
Nonetheless,
that assistance was invaluable.

00:14:27.731 --> 00:14:29.358
It could be two or three days

00:14:29.399 --> 00:14:31.128
before we'll know
if the graft will hold.

00:14:31.168 --> 00:14:34.069
In the meantime, perhaps
I should deactivate

00:14:34.104 --> 00:14:35.833
your program temporarily.

00:14:35.873 --> 00:14:37.465
Do you have to?

00:14:37.508 --> 00:14:40.136
It would slow the degradation
of your synaptic patterns.

00:14:40.177 --> 00:14:41.405
But I have so much energy.

00:14:41.445 --> 00:14:42.469
I don't know.

00:14:42.513 --> 00:14:44.879
Maybe it's the excitement
of the surgery, or...

00:14:44.915 --> 00:14:47.076
or maybe it's this new body.

00:14:47.117 --> 00:14:50.280
What I'd really like to do
is take a walk

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:52.083
and see the rest of your ship.

00:14:52.122 --> 00:14:54.818
Unfortunately,
that's not possible.

00:14:54.858 --> 00:14:57.952
However, if you're looking
for something to do,

00:14:57.995 --> 00:14:59.656
please feel free
to use my office

00:14:59.696 --> 00:15:01.323
to access our medical database.

00:15:01.365 --> 00:15:03.196
You'll find several
interesting texts

00:15:03.233 --> 00:15:04.723
on comparative endocrinology.

00:15:04.768 --> 00:15:06.030
All right.

00:15:06.069 --> 00:15:07.832
Thank you.

00:15:09.606 --> 00:15:13.633
On second thought, there is
someplace else we could go.

00:15:22.286 --> 00:15:24.083
It's wonderful.

00:15:24.121 --> 00:15:25.952
If I had a place
like this to go to,

00:15:26.056 --> 00:15:27.455
I'd be there every day.

00:15:27.491 --> 00:15:30.085
Don't your people have
recreational facilities?

00:15:30.127 --> 00:15:32.362
Congregating in groups
is strictly regulated.

00:15:32.362 --> 00:15:33.420
Congregating in groups
is strictly regulated.

00:15:33.463 --> 00:15:35.294
It's considered to be
a threat to public health.

00:15:35.331 --> 00:15:37.629
A wise policy.

00:15:37.667 --> 00:15:39.225
I suppose.

00:15:39.268 --> 00:15:41.259
Sometimes, I think my
people spend so much time

00:15:41.304 --> 00:15:42.635
trying to save lives,

00:15:42.672 --> 00:15:44.537
they don't know
how to live anymore.

00:15:44.574 --> 00:15:48.476
Doctor, aren't you going
to introduce me to your date?

00:15:48.511 --> 00:15:49.910
She is not my date.

00:15:49.946 --> 00:15:51.345
She's my patient.

00:15:53.015 --> 00:15:54.812
I'm sorry.
I didn't realize...

00:15:54.851 --> 00:15:57.911
Mr. Neelix,
this is Dr. Danara Pel.

00:15:57.954 --> 00:15:59.421
As Chief Morale Officer,

00:15:59.455 --> 00:16:02.549
may I be the first
to welcome you to Voyager.

00:16:02.592 --> 00:16:05.220
Madame, your loveliness

00:16:05.261 --> 00:16:07.923
illuminates
our dark little cavern.

00:16:07.997 --> 00:16:09.589
May I have the pleasure
of this next dance?

00:16:09.632 --> 00:16:11.566
Go away immediately.

00:16:11.601 --> 00:16:13.831
Both of you.
You're disturbing my patient.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:17.362
You are just jealous
because you cannot dance.

00:16:18.741 --> 00:16:19.708
Let's go.

00:16:19.742 --> 00:16:21.733
You're making the lady nervous.

00:16:21.778 --> 00:16:24.269
Nice to meet you.

00:16:26.149 --> 00:16:27.480
I apologize.

00:16:27.517 --> 00:16:29.815
No. They were just being nice.

00:16:29.852 --> 00:16:31.444
Irritating, isn't it?

00:16:32.588 --> 00:16:36.456
I guess I'm just not used
to... so much attention.

00:16:37.727 --> 00:16:39.661
Where I come from,

00:16:39.695 --> 00:16:41.128
when you're as sick as I am,

00:16:41.164 --> 00:16:44.964
people... healthy people...
stay away from you.

00:16:45.067 --> 00:16:47.194
I guess...

00:16:48.771 --> 00:16:50.636
I...

00:16:50.673 --> 00:16:51.833
I forgot for a second

00:16:51.874 --> 00:16:53.899
that I don't look
like that anymore.

00:16:53.943 --> 00:16:56.639
It's a natural response.

00:16:56.679 --> 00:16:59.876
All this talk about me.

00:16:59.916 --> 00:17:03.044
There's still so much
I'd like to know about you.

00:17:03.085 --> 00:17:05.349
There's not much to tell,
really.

00:17:05.388 --> 00:17:07.481
My program was developed
by Dr. Louis Zimmerman

00:17:07.523 --> 00:17:09.491
in a lab on Jupiter Station.

00:17:09.525 --> 00:17:12.926
I was activated
on stardate 48308.

00:17:12.962 --> 00:17:16.921
Since that time, I've performed
347 medical exams,

00:17:17.033 --> 00:17:21.163
healed 11 compound fractures,
performed three appendectomies

00:17:21.204 --> 00:17:23.172
and, in my greatest feat
of medical prowess,

00:17:23.206 --> 00:17:26.733
I once cured Mr. Neelix
of an acute case of the hiccups.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:29.771
You're very funny.

00:17:29.812 --> 00:17:31.109
I am?

00:17:32.715 --> 00:17:35.741
Well, several clinical studies

00:17:35.785 --> 00:17:37.719
have shown humor
to be very therapeutic.

00:17:37.753 --> 00:17:39.653
Consider it
part of your treatment.

00:17:43.192 --> 00:17:44.716
What is it?

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.955
It's, uh... just that I...

00:17:48.664 --> 00:17:50.791
I haven't laughed
in a very long time.

00:17:52.668 --> 00:17:54.465
Thank you.

00:17:58.341 --> 00:18:01.538
What did that man mean
when he said you can't "dance"?

00:18:03.246 --> 00:18:04.907
That's dancing.

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:13.111
And you can't do it?

00:18:14.223 --> 00:18:16.350
It's not part of my programming.

00:18:16.392 --> 00:18:17.791
Oh.

00:18:17.827 --> 00:18:19.089
I see.

00:18:31.974 --> 00:18:34.738
Well, Dr. Pel...

00:18:34.777 --> 00:18:36.768
Please, call me Danara.

00:18:36.812 --> 00:18:40.111
As you wish... Danara.

00:18:40.149 --> 00:18:42.310
And what about you?

00:18:42.351 --> 00:18:43.841
What should I call you?

00:18:43.886 --> 00:18:45.854
Well, as I said...

00:18:45.888 --> 00:18:47.583
I know.
You don't have a name.

00:18:49.692 --> 00:18:51.853
Would it be all right
if I gave you one?

00:18:51.894 --> 00:18:54.328
Well, I...

00:18:54.363 --> 00:18:55.728
How about...

00:18:57.333 --> 00:18:59.460
Shmullus?

00:19:01.270 --> 00:19:02.396
Shmullus?

00:19:02.438 --> 00:19:04.303
It was my uncle's name.

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:07.104
He used to make me laugh, too.

00:19:09.512 --> 00:19:11.139
Doctor...

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.045
Shmullus.

00:19:13.082 --> 00:19:16.017
I think I like
the sound of that.

00:19:33.269 --> 00:19:34.759
Well...

00:19:35.871 --> 00:19:37.304
here we are.

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:39.205
Yes.

00:19:39.241 --> 00:19:40.765
Here we are.

00:19:42.144 --> 00:19:43.441
Danara, I think we should...

00:19:43.479 --> 00:19:44.571
Yes?

00:19:44.614 --> 00:19:46.946
Deactivate your program
for at least eight hours.

00:19:48.217 --> 00:19:49.582
If you think it's best.

00:19:49.619 --> 00:19:51.382
I do.

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:52.785
All right, then.

00:19:52.822 --> 00:19:54.119
All right.

00:19:54.156 --> 00:19:55.123
Computer...

00:19:55.157 --> 00:19:56.818
- Shmullus?
- Yes?

00:19:58.294 --> 00:20:01.058
I had a wonderful time.

00:20:03.766 --> 00:20:05.961
I'm pleased.

00:20:06.068 --> 00:20:08.093
Thank you...

00:20:08.137 --> 00:20:09.832
for...

00:20:09.872 --> 00:20:11.499
everything.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:13.633
Thank you for...

00:20:15.311 --> 00:20:16.710
giving me a name.

00:20:30.326 --> 00:20:32.817
Uh... well...

00:20:32.862 --> 00:20:34.796
good night, Danara.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:37.298
Good night...

00:20:37.333 --> 00:20:38.766
Shmullus.

00:20:40.603 --> 00:20:45.768
Computer, deactivate
Vidiian program Alpha.

00:21:09.131 --> 00:21:11.156
Mind if I join you?

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:22.468
So how are things, Tom?

00:21:22.511 --> 00:21:24.308
Excuse me?

00:21:24.346 --> 00:21:25.973
How have you been
feeling lately?

00:21:26.048 --> 00:21:27.515
Is something bothering you?

00:21:30.419 --> 00:21:31.909
Oh, no offense, Commander,

00:21:31.954 --> 00:21:35.321
but why the sudden concern
for my feelings?

00:21:35.357 --> 00:21:37.086
Well, you've been moody lately,

00:21:37.126 --> 00:21:38.457
indifferent to your duties.

00:21:38.494 --> 00:21:40.621
To be honest,
you don't seem to be

00:21:40.663 --> 00:21:42.790
taking your job very seriously.

00:21:42.832 --> 00:21:43.992
If you've got a problem,

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:45.567
I'd like to know what it is.

00:21:48.838 --> 00:21:51.272
Yeah, I've got a problem.

00:21:51.307 --> 00:21:53.207
My problem is you.

00:21:57.246 --> 00:21:58.975
You care to elaborate?

00:21:59.014 --> 00:22:02.711
You tell me
I don't take my job seriously,

00:22:02.752 --> 00:22:05.084
but half the time,
you don't let me do my job.

00:22:05.121 --> 00:22:06.713
What's that supposed to mean?

00:22:06.756 --> 00:22:09.247
It means that you
don't trust my judgment.

00:22:09.291 --> 00:22:11.191
You don't allow me
to take initiative.

00:22:11.227 --> 00:22:12.194
Remember last week?

00:22:12.228 --> 00:22:13.661
I suggested
that we might save time

00:22:13.696 --> 00:22:15.527
by traveling through
that emissions nebula.

00:22:15.564 --> 00:22:17.088
But what did you say?

00:22:17.133 --> 00:22:20.569
"Oh, no, that's not the way we
do things on this ship."

00:22:20.603 --> 00:22:23.299
Look, sometimes I'm not going
to agree with your suggestions,

00:22:23.339 --> 00:22:25.864
but making decisions
is part of being a leader.

00:22:25.908 --> 00:22:27.967
Maybe someday
you'll understand that.

00:22:28.077 --> 00:22:30.272
Being a leader also means
knowing when to give your people

00:22:30.312 --> 00:22:32.974
a little leeway
and let them be creative.

00:22:33.015 --> 00:22:35.142
We might as well put this ship
on autopilot

00:22:35.184 --> 00:22:37.379
for all the freedom
you give me to do my job.

00:22:37.419 --> 00:22:40.252
I didn't come here for a lecture
from you on how to do my job.

00:22:40.289 --> 00:22:42.985
Yeah, well, I know you don't put
much stock in my opinion,

00:22:43.025 --> 00:22:46.324
so maybe you should talk
to some of these people.

00:22:46.362 --> 00:22:47.829
Because I'm not the only one
around here

00:22:47.863 --> 00:22:49.057
who's got a problem with you.

00:22:50.166 --> 00:22:52.691
Now, if there's nothing else...

00:22:52.735 --> 00:22:54.134
sir...

00:22:54.170 --> 00:22:55.637
I'd like to be excused.

00:22:58.607 --> 00:23:00.700
Sure, Paris.

00:23:00.743 --> 00:23:02.108
You're excused.

00:23:08.651 --> 00:23:11.518
Dissension among
the Voyager crew.

00:23:11.554 --> 00:23:14.955
Maje Culluh will find that
very interesting.

00:23:15.057 --> 00:23:16.615
Good work, Mr. Jonas.

00:23:16.659 --> 00:23:18.627
Now, there's something else
we'd like you to do.

00:23:18.661 --> 00:23:22.358
We want you to create a small
accident, which will damage

00:23:22.398 --> 00:23:23.695
Voyager's warp coils.

00:23:23.732 --> 00:23:24.960
Why?

00:23:25.034 --> 00:23:27.696
There's no need to concern
yourself with that.

00:23:27.736 --> 00:23:31.137
You just... plan the accident.

00:23:31.173 --> 00:23:32.540
We'll let you know exactly
when we want it to happen.

00:23:32.540 --> 00:23:34.940
We'll let you know exactly
when we want it to happen.

00:23:34.975 --> 00:23:37.944
Do we understand each other?

00:23:37.978 --> 00:23:40.071
I want to talk to Seska.

00:23:40.114 --> 00:23:41.479
I'm afraid Maje Culluh...

00:23:41.515 --> 00:23:42.641
You tell Maje Culluh

00:23:42.683 --> 00:23:44.617
that I won't do anything
to damage Voyager,

00:23:44.652 --> 00:23:46.415
and if he has
a problem with that,

00:23:46.453 --> 00:23:48.478
tell him to have
Seska contact me.

00:23:54.695 --> 00:23:55.992
Doctor, when you have a minute.

00:23:56.030 --> 00:23:58.658
I'm running a level-2
self-diagnostic right now.

00:23:58.699 --> 00:24:00.530
I'll be there
as soon as I'm finished.

00:24:00.568 --> 00:24:02.559
Why are you running
a diagnostic?

00:24:02.603 --> 00:24:05.299
I've been experiencing
periodic lapses in concentration

00:24:05.339 --> 00:24:07.398
and difficulty handling objects.

00:24:07.441 --> 00:24:09.204
There may be a malfunction

00:24:09.243 --> 00:24:11.404
in my tactile acuity subroutine.

00:24:11.445 --> 00:24:12.878
How long has this been going on?

00:24:12.913 --> 00:24:14.505
About two or three days.

00:24:14.548 --> 00:24:16.448
Since Danara came aboard.

00:24:16.483 --> 00:24:18.383
What's your point?

00:24:18.419 --> 00:24:20.819
Maybe she's the reason
you're feeling this way.

00:24:20.854 --> 00:24:22.947
I fail to see a connection.

00:24:23.023 --> 00:24:25.491
Maybe you're attracted to her.

00:24:27.227 --> 00:24:29.422
I told you,
my program's malfunctioning.

00:24:29.463 --> 00:24:31.556
Romance is not a malfunction.

00:24:31.599 --> 00:24:33.396
Romance is not part
of my programming.

00:24:33.434 --> 00:24:35.595
Your programming's adaptive,
isn't it?

00:24:35.636 --> 00:24:36.694
Yes.

00:24:36.737 --> 00:24:38.432
Then I'd say it's adapting.

00:24:38.472 --> 00:24:40.770
What if...

00:24:43.377 --> 00:24:46.210
I don't want it
to adapt right now?

00:24:46.246 --> 00:24:47.873
Why wouldn't you?

00:24:47.915 --> 00:24:50.679
Because I don't like
what's happening to me.

00:24:55.689 --> 00:25:00.149
I'm used to being in control
of my faculties...

00:25:00.194 --> 00:25:03.561
confident of my decisions.

00:25:03.597 --> 00:25:05.758
But lately...

00:25:05.799 --> 00:25:07.858
whenever Danara's program
is deactivated

00:25:07.901 --> 00:25:09.994
and I should be
concentrating on my work...

00:25:11.639 --> 00:25:14.437
I find myself thinking
of nothing but her.

00:25:14.475 --> 00:25:16.602
Why don't you reactivate her?

00:25:16.644 --> 00:25:20.136
Because whenever I do that,
I suddenly feel...

00:25:20.180 --> 00:25:25.550
unsettled... unsure of myself,
and I have no idea what to say.

00:25:27.921 --> 00:25:30.287
Why would people
seek out situations

00:25:30.324 --> 00:25:32.724
which induce
such unpleasant symptoms?

00:25:32.760 --> 00:25:35.058
Because when the other person
feels the same way you do,

00:25:35.095 --> 00:25:37.325
it's the most wonderful
thing in life.

00:25:41.869 --> 00:25:43.461
Suppose...

00:25:43.504 --> 00:25:44.471
hypothetically

00:25:44.505 --> 00:25:45.563
of course...

00:25:45.606 --> 00:25:46.971
Of course.

00:25:50.210 --> 00:25:52.906
I wanted to pursue
that possibility.

00:25:52.946 --> 00:25:54.208
How would I proceed?

00:25:54.248 --> 00:25:56.045
You'd have to tell her
how you feel.

00:25:57.351 --> 00:25:58.978
That's it?

00:25:59.086 --> 00:26:01.646
Just... tell her how I feel?

00:26:01.689 --> 00:26:04.522
Otherwise, you may never know
how she feels.

00:26:11.231 --> 00:26:13.927
I'm going to try stimulating
your motor neurons.

00:26:14.968 --> 00:26:16.936
Well, the nucleus cuneatus

00:26:17.037 --> 00:26:19.130
appears to be functioning
normally.

00:26:19.173 --> 00:26:24.167
And now for the anterior
thalamic pathway.

00:26:25.746 --> 00:26:27.577
Excellent.

00:26:27.614 --> 00:26:30.174
By the way, Danara,
I've been meaning to tell you...

00:26:30.217 --> 00:26:31.184
Yes?

00:26:31.218 --> 00:26:32.617
I'm romantically attracted
to you

00:26:32.653 --> 00:26:34.621
and wanted to know
if you felt the same way.

00:26:39.593 --> 00:26:41.185
Is something wrong?

00:26:41.228 --> 00:26:44.026
No. I...

00:26:45.499 --> 00:26:47.763
Did you understand what I said?

00:26:47.801 --> 00:26:49.860
Yes.

00:26:49.903 --> 00:26:51.700
Well?

00:26:51.739 --> 00:26:54.299
Doctor, maybe now
isn't the time to...

00:26:54.341 --> 00:26:56.775
Excuse me, Kes.
I was speaking to Danara.

00:27:00.581 --> 00:27:05.814
I think it's best if we keep our
relationship... professional.

00:27:14.862 --> 00:27:16.227
Well...

00:27:17.931 --> 00:27:20.798
I'm going to...

00:27:20.834 --> 00:27:25.066
try stimulating
the posterior sciatic nerve.

00:27:35.783 --> 00:27:37.944
Doc, what brings you here?

00:27:37.985 --> 00:27:39.953
Is somebody sick?

00:27:39.987 --> 00:27:41.955
Actually, Mr. Paris,
I was looking for you.

00:27:41.989 --> 00:27:43.616
Oh.

00:27:43.657 --> 00:27:45.352
Well, pull up a chair.

00:27:45.392 --> 00:27:46.916
Mr. Paris,

00:27:46.960 --> 00:27:48.621
I assume you've had a
great deal of experience

00:27:48.662 --> 00:27:50.186
being rejected by women.

00:27:50.230 --> 00:27:51.891
Oh, thanks a lot, Doc.

00:27:51.932 --> 00:27:53.900
What I'd like to know is:

00:27:53.934 --> 00:27:55.526
What does one do to recover

00:27:55.569 --> 00:27:58.629
from the unpleasant symptoms
of romantic rejection?

00:27:58.672 --> 00:28:01.163
Why the sudden interest
in romance?

00:28:01.208 --> 00:28:02.232
I can't tell you.

00:28:02.276 --> 00:28:05.905
It's a matter of doctor/
patient confidentiality.

00:28:05.946 --> 00:28:08.244
Ah.

00:28:08.282 --> 00:28:10.546
All right, well, let's see.

00:28:13.787 --> 00:28:15.880
Sometimes there's
not a lot you can do

00:28:15.923 --> 00:28:18.414
to get over a woman
you really care about.

00:28:21.028 --> 00:28:23.929
I remember when Susie Crabtree
dumped me

00:28:23.964 --> 00:28:27.127
back in my first year
at the Academy.

00:28:27.167 --> 00:28:29.135
I broke out in hives.

00:28:29.169 --> 00:28:30.568
Couldn't get out of bed
for a week.

00:28:30.604 --> 00:28:32.936
I almost failed
Stellar Cartography.

00:28:33.040 --> 00:28:36.737
I walked around in a daze
for the rest of that year.

00:28:36.777 --> 00:28:42.875
Of course, the first one is
always the hardest to get over.

00:28:44.852 --> 00:28:46.752
I see.

00:28:46.787 --> 00:28:49.779
But... eventually,

00:28:49.823 --> 00:28:52.656
you start thinking
about her less and less,

00:28:52.693 --> 00:28:55.890
until finally,
without realizing it,

00:28:55.929 --> 00:28:57.692
she's not on your mind anymore.

00:28:57.731 --> 00:29:00.791
So the symptoms do subside
over time?

00:29:02.102 --> 00:29:03.797
For the most part.

00:29:03.837 --> 00:29:09.275
But every now and then,
even years later,

00:29:09.309 --> 00:29:10.901
something reminds you of her...

00:29:11.011 --> 00:29:15.209
a certain smell,
a few notes of a song...

00:29:15.249 --> 00:29:16.238
and suddenly you feel

00:29:16.283 --> 00:29:17.910
just as bad as the day
she told you

00:29:17.985 --> 00:29:19.646
she never wanted
to see you again.

00:29:20.754 --> 00:29:23.518
If you want to know
the honest truth, Doc,

00:29:23.557 --> 00:29:26.583
you never completely get over
a woman you really cared about.

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:31.292
Wait a minute.

00:29:31.331 --> 00:29:34.823
Doc, we're not talking
about you, are we?

00:29:36.036 --> 00:29:38.368
I told you, it was confidential.

00:29:38.405 --> 00:29:41.932
Oh, boy, you've got it bad.

00:29:42.009 --> 00:29:44.944
Look, Doc, I don't
mean to intrude,

00:29:45.045 --> 00:29:47.741
but if you tell me what's
going on, maybe I can help.

00:30:02.863 --> 00:30:04.956
Hello, Kes.

00:30:05.032 --> 00:30:07.000
Are you feeling all right?

00:30:08.535 --> 00:30:09.934
I'm fine.

00:30:09.970 --> 00:30:13.167
I'm just... waiting
for the Doctor.

00:30:13.206 --> 00:30:14.537
Oh.

00:30:14.574 --> 00:30:15.939
He's been gone a long time.

00:30:19.546 --> 00:30:21.571
You really like him, don't you?

00:30:24.117 --> 00:30:26.381
Then... why didn't you tell him

00:30:26.420 --> 00:30:27.819
that you felt the same way

00:30:27.854 --> 00:30:30.345
when he told you that he
was attracted to you?

00:30:30.390 --> 00:30:32.449
I don't know.
It all happened so fast.

00:30:32.492 --> 00:30:33.789
He just blurted it out.

00:30:33.827 --> 00:30:36.295
He's very blunt.

00:30:36.330 --> 00:30:37.797
You shouldn't
take it personally.

00:30:37.831 --> 00:30:38.991
How could he possibly have

00:30:39.099 --> 00:30:41.431
those kinds
of feelings about me?

00:30:41.468 --> 00:30:44.164
Maybe because
you're a compassionate person,

00:30:44.204 --> 00:30:46.104
a brilliant doctor,

00:30:46.139 --> 00:30:47.504
you appreciate his humor...

00:30:47.541 --> 00:30:48.906
Should I go on?

00:30:48.942 --> 00:30:50.773
Please don't.

00:30:50.811 --> 00:30:53.006
One thing
you're not very good at

00:30:53.113 --> 00:30:55.013
is accepting a compliment.

00:30:55.048 --> 00:30:57.881
The next time someone has
something nice to say about you

00:30:57.918 --> 00:31:00.580
maybe you should just
take them at their word

00:31:00.620 --> 00:31:01.848
and feel good about yourself.

00:31:03.557 --> 00:31:05.718
It's not easy to feel
good about yourself

00:31:05.759 --> 00:31:08.455
when you're used to living
your life... like that.

00:31:08.495 --> 00:31:11.726
Danara, I can't pretend to know
what your life's been like,

00:31:11.765 --> 00:31:13.426
but I do know
there's nothing sadder

00:31:13.467 --> 00:31:15.401
than a missed opportunity.

00:31:17.004 --> 00:31:18.972
Maybe what you
and the Doctor need

00:31:19.072 --> 00:31:21.563
is to spend some time
together... alone.

00:31:25.078 --> 00:31:27.205
It sounds to me
like she might just be shy.

00:31:27.247 --> 00:31:29.715
I think you scared her off.

00:31:29.750 --> 00:31:31.012
I did?

00:31:32.419 --> 00:31:34.487
Your approach is all wrong.

00:31:35.855 --> 00:31:37.846
Well, what would be
the right approach?

00:31:37.890 --> 00:31:40.415
Women like romance.

00:31:40.459 --> 00:31:42.154
They want men
to make an effort...

00:31:42.194 --> 00:31:43.718
take them someplace special.

00:31:45.231 --> 00:31:46.528
Where would I take her?

00:31:49.969 --> 00:31:51.698
Come with me, Doc.

00:31:51.737 --> 00:31:53.068
I've got an idea.

00:31:58.978 --> 00:32:04.280
Doctor's Personal Log,
Stardate 49504.3.

00:32:04.316 --> 00:32:06.409
Inaugural entry.

00:32:06.452 --> 00:32:08.477
Kes and Mr. Paris have conspired

00:32:08.521 --> 00:32:10.148
to get Danara and me
alone together

00:32:10.189 --> 00:32:12.714
in a place
Paris considers romantic.

00:32:12.758 --> 00:32:16.353
I've never felt more... uneasy.

00:32:30.009 --> 00:32:31.977
I wasn't sure you were coming.

00:32:32.011 --> 00:32:33.501
Neither was I.

00:32:33.546 --> 00:32:34.638
If you don't want to be here...

00:32:34.680 --> 00:32:35.806
No.

00:32:35.848 --> 00:32:37.008
I do.

00:32:40.452 --> 00:32:42.579
Where are we exactly?

00:32:42.621 --> 00:32:44.748
On a planet called Mars.

00:32:44.790 --> 00:32:46.985
Inside a primitive
land-based vehicle.

00:32:47.026 --> 00:32:48.926
It's called a '57 Chevy.

00:32:48.961 --> 00:32:51.327
Mr. Paris is quite
an automobile aficionado.

00:32:51.363 --> 00:32:53.126
This is his program.

00:32:56.135 --> 00:32:58.000
What is it that we're
supposed to be doing?

00:33:00.506 --> 00:33:04.135
I believe it's called...
parking.

00:33:07.346 --> 00:33:09.337
I almost forgot.

00:33:10.616 --> 00:33:12.174
These are for you.

00:33:12.217 --> 00:33:14.845
Thank you.

00:33:14.887 --> 00:33:17.981
You're... you're
very... very thoughtful.

00:33:26.098 --> 00:33:28.566
My prayer...

00:33:29.735 --> 00:33:32.226
I downloaded
a new dancing subroutine

00:33:32.271 --> 00:33:33.533
into my program this morning.

00:33:33.572 --> 00:33:35.301
Would you like
to get out and try it?

00:33:35.341 --> 00:33:37.309
Actually...

00:33:37.343 --> 00:33:41.973
I wouldn't mind just...
sitting here for a while.

00:33:42.047 --> 00:33:43.344
You wouldn't?

00:33:45.351 --> 00:33:47.148
Those moons and star formations

00:33:47.186 --> 00:33:50.349
are so different from anything
I've ever seen before.

00:33:50.389 --> 00:33:52.914
Well, if you're interested,

00:33:52.958 --> 00:33:55.688
I could point out a few
astronomical highlights.

00:33:58.364 --> 00:34:00.389
You see that bluish planet
there...

00:34:00.432 --> 00:34:02.730
that's called "Earth."

00:34:02.768 --> 00:34:04.668
It's where Starfleet
Headquarters is located.

00:34:04.703 --> 00:34:07.501
With the world far away...

00:34:07.539 --> 00:34:11.236
And over... there
that's "Cygnus."

00:34:11.276 --> 00:34:12.743
And there...

00:34:12.778 --> 00:34:15.042
that constellation
is called "Hercules,"

00:34:15.080 --> 00:34:17.446
named after a character
in ancient Greek myth.

00:34:17.483 --> 00:34:18.882
Hippocrates was also a Greek.

00:34:18.917 --> 00:34:20.043
He was the father of...

00:34:20.085 --> 00:34:22.212
Tonight...

00:34:22.254 --> 00:34:23.949
Earth medicine.

00:34:23.989 --> 00:34:27.425
While our heart are aglow...

00:34:27.459 --> 00:34:29.393
And that cluster over there...

00:34:29.428 --> 00:34:32.761
that's... called the "Pleiades."

00:34:32.798 --> 00:34:43.231
Oh, tell me the words
that I'm longing to know

00:34:45.544 --> 00:34:50.504
My prayer

00:34:50.549 --> 00:34:55.612
And the answer you give

00:34:58.323 --> 00:35:02.453
May they still be the same

00:35:05.130 --> 00:35:11.069
For as long as we live

00:35:11.103 --> 00:35:15.836
That you'll always be there...

00:35:23.649 --> 00:35:25.378
Sorry I'm late.

00:35:25.417 --> 00:35:26.850
That's all right, Mr. Paris.

00:35:26.885 --> 00:35:27.852
We don't need you.

00:35:27.886 --> 00:35:30.821
Mr. Grimes has taken
your place at conn.

00:35:32.191 --> 00:35:33.658
But it's my shift.

00:35:33.692 --> 00:35:35.660
Not today it isn't.

00:35:35.694 --> 00:35:38.857
What, because I was
ten minutes late?

00:35:38.897 --> 00:35:40.455
That's right.

00:35:42.334 --> 00:35:43.301
Captain...

00:35:43.335 --> 00:35:44.495
Don't look at me, Mr. Paris.

00:35:44.536 --> 00:35:47.562
Commander Chakotay has complete
discretion in this matter.

00:35:52.544 --> 00:35:55.809
So, when should I
report back for duty?

00:35:55.848 --> 00:35:59.545
When you decide to start
taking your job seriously,

00:35:59.585 --> 00:36:00.882
we'll discuss it.

00:36:00.919 --> 00:36:02.284
But right now, you're dismissed.

00:36:02.321 --> 00:36:04.585
Get your hands off me!

00:36:10.129 --> 00:36:11.562
Mr. Tuvok.

00:36:11.597 --> 00:36:12.928
Yes, Captain.

00:36:13.031 --> 00:36:16.296
Please escort Mr. Paris
to the brig.

00:36:37.222 --> 00:36:39.952
Oh, boy, am I glad to see you.

00:36:40.025 --> 00:36:42.255
I wasn't even sure if they were
giving you my messages.

00:36:42.294 --> 00:36:43.727
I've gotten them all, Mike.

00:36:43.762 --> 00:36:45.252
You've been very helpful.

00:36:46.665 --> 00:36:50.066
Do you know
what they're asking me to do?

00:36:50.102 --> 00:36:51.694
You mean about the warp coils?

00:36:51.737 --> 00:36:53.466
I was thinking you could do it

00:36:53.505 --> 00:36:56.838
by forcing the magnetic
constrictors out of alignment.

00:36:56.875 --> 00:36:58.968
Look, Seska, I don't mind
feeding you information,

00:36:59.011 --> 00:37:01.343
but if you're planning
some kind of attack...

00:37:01.380 --> 00:37:05.373
I have no intention of raising
my child on a Kazon ship!

00:37:05.417 --> 00:37:07.783
One way or another,
I'm going to take Voyager.

00:37:07.820 --> 00:37:09.720
You can either help me
or you can suffer

00:37:09.755 --> 00:37:11.484
along with Janeway
and the others.

00:37:13.926 --> 00:37:16.417
Don't worry, Mike.

00:37:16.461 --> 00:37:18.827
Everything's been planned
to the letter.

00:37:18.864 --> 00:37:21.389
Here's how it's going to work.

00:37:21.433 --> 00:37:26.496
We'll be waiting for you
on a planet called Hemikek IV.

00:37:28.073 --> 00:37:32.339
Doctor's Personal Log,
Stardate 49507.2.

00:37:32.377 --> 00:37:34.504
The more time I spend
with Danara,

00:37:34.546 --> 00:37:37.242
the more my programming
continues to adapt.

00:37:37.282 --> 00:37:39.682
I look forward to perfecting
my romantic skills

00:37:39.718 --> 00:37:42.312
once we've completed
the synaptic transfer.

00:37:42.354 --> 00:37:45.050
Set the delta band frequency
of the holo-emitter

00:37:45.090 --> 00:37:46.057
to seven terahertz.

00:37:46.091 --> 00:37:47.558
Seven terahertz.

00:37:50.762 --> 00:37:52.525
Wait a minute.

00:37:52.564 --> 00:37:55.829
Did you administer the cervaline
as I instructed?

00:37:55.868 --> 00:37:58.234
500 milligrams every four hours.

00:37:58.270 --> 00:37:59.794
I don't understand it.

00:37:59.838 --> 00:38:00.930
What's wrong?

00:38:00.973 --> 00:38:05.137
The brain... your brain...
it's rejecting the graft.

00:38:05.177 --> 00:38:07.771
We can't go through
with the transfer.

00:38:14.853 --> 00:38:17.447
I'm detecting elevated
levels of nytoxinol.

00:38:17.489 --> 00:38:18.751
Where could that have come from?

00:38:18.790 --> 00:38:20.314
Is it possible
you made an error?

00:38:20.359 --> 00:38:22.384
Administered nytoxinol
instead of cervaline?

00:38:22.427 --> 00:38:25.396
No, I don't think so.

00:38:25.430 --> 00:38:27.227
But here's the hypospray I used.

00:38:27.266 --> 00:38:28.665
Check for yourself.

00:38:28.700 --> 00:38:30.930
You're correct.
It's cervaline.

00:38:30.969 --> 00:38:32.334
Has anyone else been in Sick Bay

00:38:32.371 --> 00:38:34.601
during the last 24 hours
other than you and Danara?

00:38:34.640 --> 00:38:36.471
Crewman Foster came in
for some analgesic

00:38:36.508 --> 00:38:38.135
and Ensign Wildman was here

00:38:38.176 --> 00:38:40.440
for her regular prenatal visit.
Why?

00:38:40.479 --> 00:38:41.446
Because, if the nytoxinol

00:38:41.480 --> 00:38:42.742
was not administered
by accident,

00:38:42.781 --> 00:38:43.839
I can only conclude

00:38:43.882 --> 00:38:45.850
that someone is deliberately
trying to kill Danara.

00:38:45.884 --> 00:38:47.784
Who would want to kill her?

00:38:47.819 --> 00:38:49.548
Perhaps someone who bears
ill will toward Vidiians.

00:38:49.588 --> 00:38:50.816
Whoever it is,
I intend to find out.

00:38:50.856 --> 00:38:51.823
I'm calling Lieutenant Tuvok.

00:38:51.857 --> 00:38:53.654
Please don't do that.

00:38:53.692 --> 00:38:54.659
We have to find out

00:38:54.693 --> 00:38:56.684
who's trying
to obstruct your recovery.

00:38:56.728 --> 00:38:59.288
I administered the nytoxinol.

00:39:01.800 --> 00:39:03.199
Didn't you know
it would kill you?

00:39:03.235 --> 00:39:04.896
You mean kill her.

00:39:04.970 --> 00:39:05.902
She is you.

00:39:06.004 --> 00:39:06.902
Was me.

00:39:06.939 --> 00:39:08.964
I don't ever want
to be her again.

00:39:14.446 --> 00:39:16.437
What are you doing?

00:39:16.481 --> 00:39:17.880
Looking for the cervaline.

00:39:17.916 --> 00:39:19.907
I have to reduce the rate
of tissue rejection

00:39:20.018 --> 00:39:21.042
before it's too late.

00:39:21.119 --> 00:39:22.916
Kes, would you excuse us?

00:39:29.225 --> 00:39:30.920
I don't want to go through
with the transfer.

00:39:30.994 --> 00:39:32.461
If we don't get
your neural patterns

00:39:32.495 --> 00:39:33.519
out of the holo-buffer,

00:39:33.563 --> 00:39:35.224
you'll be brain dead
in a matter of days.

00:39:35.264 --> 00:39:36.754
I can't let that happen.

00:39:36.799 --> 00:39:39.632
I'd rather live two more
days like this with you

00:39:39.669 --> 00:39:40.931
than go on
for who knows how long,

00:39:41.004 --> 00:39:42.232
wasting away a piece at a time.

00:39:42.271 --> 00:39:44.432
It's my duty to keep you alive.

00:39:44.474 --> 00:39:45.839
I thought you were
more than my doctor.

00:39:45.875 --> 00:39:46.842
I thought you were my friend.

00:39:46.876 --> 00:39:48.400
I am your friend.

00:39:48.444 --> 00:39:51.936
What kind of friend would ask me
to go on living like this?

00:39:52.015 --> 00:39:53.175
And for what?

00:39:53.216 --> 00:39:54.740
So that I can go back to a world

00:39:54.784 --> 00:39:56.547
where everyone I ever loved
has died,

00:39:56.586 --> 00:39:59.214
where almost everyone I meet
is going to die?

00:39:59.255 --> 00:40:00.222
You're a doctor.

00:40:00.256 --> 00:40:01.223
You can help them.

00:40:01.257 --> 00:40:02.383
I can't help them.

00:40:02.425 --> 00:40:03.483
I can't cure them.

00:40:03.526 --> 00:40:06.552
All I can do
is prolong their suffering...

00:40:06.596 --> 00:40:09.724
just like you want
to do to me now.

00:40:09.766 --> 00:40:11.927
Danara...

00:40:14.437 --> 00:40:16.496
I have no desire
to see you suffer.

00:40:16.539 --> 00:40:19.303
Do you know what it's like?
Do you?

00:40:19.342 --> 00:40:20.309
No, but...

00:40:20.343 --> 00:40:21.810
What it's like to be
a nine-year-old child

00:40:21.844 --> 00:40:23.175
and suddenly your best friend

00:40:23.212 --> 00:40:25.180
doesn't want to come
to your house anymore.

00:40:25.214 --> 00:40:27.978
And when you ask
your mother why...

00:40:28.051 --> 00:40:30.884
"Why won't Mala come
and play with me anymore?"

00:40:30.920 --> 00:40:32.911
And she tells you
it's because...

00:40:34.691 --> 00:40:38.627
it's because the other children
are afraid of you.

00:40:47.437 --> 00:40:48.927
Listen to me.

00:40:48.971 --> 00:40:52.737
Before I met you,
I was just a disease.

00:40:52.775 --> 00:40:55.642
But now, everything's different.

00:40:55.678 --> 00:40:57.009
When people look at me,

00:40:57.080 --> 00:40:59.048
they don't see a disease
anymore.

00:41:01.951 --> 00:41:04.215
They see a woman,

00:41:04.253 --> 00:41:06.517
a woman you made,

00:41:06.556 --> 00:41:08.285
a woman you love,

00:41:08.324 --> 00:41:10.656
a woman you're not
afraid to touch.

00:41:10.693 --> 00:41:14.151
Danara, I was never
afraid to touch you.

00:41:14.197 --> 00:41:16.631
Why? Because you're a doctor?

00:41:16.666 --> 00:41:18.793
Because I love you.

00:41:18.835 --> 00:41:20.962
You say that now,

00:41:21.070 --> 00:41:24.096
but if I go through
with the transfer...

00:41:24.140 --> 00:41:26.506
If you go through
with the transfer?

00:41:26.542 --> 00:41:28.942
I will be sick again...

00:41:28.978 --> 00:41:30.468
and ugly.

00:41:30.513 --> 00:41:32.640
Danara, you're not ugly.
You're simply ill.

00:41:33.683 --> 00:41:37.278
Please, stop patronizing me!

00:41:39.222 --> 00:41:41.782
I know how people see me.

00:41:41.824 --> 00:41:44.816
Danara, do you think
if you go back

00:41:44.861 --> 00:41:47.352
into your own body,
I'll feel different about you?

00:41:47.396 --> 00:41:48.385
Won't you?

00:41:48.431 --> 00:41:49.523
Listen to me.

00:41:49.565 --> 00:41:52.432
Nothing could ever change
the way I feel about you...

00:41:52.468 --> 00:41:55.835
not a few scars,
not some diseased skin, nothing.

00:41:55.872 --> 00:41:58.705
You have given me
the most extraordinary gift

00:41:58.741 --> 00:42:00.265
that anyone has ever given me.

00:42:00.309 --> 00:42:01.901
You brought me to this ship

00:42:01.944 --> 00:42:04.674
where no one is sick,
and people are friendly.

00:42:04.714 --> 00:42:08.411
You've made me
healthy and beautiful.

00:42:08.451 --> 00:42:12.114
I don't want to go back
to the way things were.

00:42:13.756 --> 00:42:18.784
You said, before you knew me,
that you were just a disease.

00:42:18.828 --> 00:42:21.956
Well, before you, I was just
a projection of photons

00:42:22.031 --> 00:42:24.192
held together by force fields,

00:42:24.233 --> 00:42:27.225
a computerized physician
doing a job,

00:42:27.270 --> 00:42:28.794
doing it exceptionally well,
of course,

00:42:28.838 --> 00:42:33.605
but still, it was... just
a profession, not a life.

00:42:33.643 --> 00:42:38.239
But now that you're here,
and my programming has adapted,

00:42:38.281 --> 00:42:40.408
I'm not just working anymore.

00:42:40.449 --> 00:42:43.145
I'm living,
learning what it means...

00:42:43.186 --> 00:42:45.518
to be with someone,
to love someone.

00:42:45.555 --> 00:42:50.356
I don't think I can go back
to the way things were either.

00:42:52.728 --> 00:42:56.164
Danara, please...

00:42:56.199 --> 00:42:58.724
don't die.

00:42:58.768 --> 00:43:01.737
I want us to be together.

00:43:01.771 --> 00:43:04.262
So do I.

00:43:06.609 --> 00:43:09.271
But if you put me back
into that body,

00:43:09.312 --> 00:43:13.806
I'll have to go home...
and help my people.

00:43:13.850 --> 00:43:15.249
I know.

00:43:15.284 --> 00:43:18.310
But we'd still have
two weeks together

00:43:18.354 --> 00:43:21.255
before we reached your colony.

00:43:24.160 --> 00:43:30.121
Danara, please, be with me
for as long as you can.

00:44:32.228 --> 00:44:37.894
Computer, play music program
Doctor-alpha.
